            <div xml:id="d874">

                <pb facs="0813" n="713" xml:id="pg713"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">661.4116/44: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-06-08T19:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 8, 1920—7
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 8—5:28 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>909. My 905.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d874-f1"/> One. I now learn officially but
                    informally from the Foreign Office that there has been no resumption of trade
                    with Soviet Russia and that shipments of commodities from this country to
                    Russian destination are legally forbidden. Customs authorities have instructions
                    prevent exportation of any consignments of this character unless export licenses
                    accompany them which latter Board of Trade has consistently refused. …</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
